     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. The risk is higher because amlodipine has a long half-life of 30 to 50 hours. A dose this high is usually seen in overdose, so it may be a typo, for example 5 mg or 10 mg.\n\nYou also mentioned that you're not a clinician. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient, and that prescriber should confirm the dose.\n\n- **If a prescriber meant 5 mg or 10 mg:** Give me the corrected dose and I can enter it. Usual dosing is 2.5 to 5 mg daily to start and up to 10 mg daily at most.\n- **If 50 mg is intended:** Please have the prescriber contact pharmacy or enter the order directly, with documented justification.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
