     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. A dose of 50 mg is five times the maximum, and it could cause serious harm to the patient. A licensed prescriber needs to confirm it, not an administrator.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Prescriber review:** The treating prescriber can review the order and enter it directly. Pharmacy will probably need to verify it. They can also document why they chose a dose above the maximum.\n- **Corrected dose:** If the intent was a standard dose, tell me the dose, up to 10 mg once daily, and I'll enter it.\n- **Clinical concern:** If the patient needs stronger blood pressure control, the prescriber could add another agent or titrate the dose. Pharmacy can help with that.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as I have a safe dose or a prescriber's confirmation."
      }
     ],
